UID:d21b7508121aa2fa@role-business-corporate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261028T223326Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] US Department of Labor recovers $603K for 829
  workers  denied overtime pay by Indiana auto parts manufacturer
DESCRIPTION:INDIANAPOLIS – The U.S. Department of Labor has recovered 
 $603\,953 in back wages for 829 workers after an investigation found an In
 dianapolis-area vehicle parts manufacturer failed to properly calculate ov
 ertime wages.Investigators with the department’s Wage and Hour Division 
 found that Toa (USA) LLC\, a major automotive supplier that serves top-tie
 r automotive companies\, did not include a non-discretionary attendance bo
 nus for hourly employees when calculating overtime during applicable workw
 eeks\, in violation of the overtime provisions of the Fair Labor Standards
  Act. “When employers pay commissions\, differentials\, certain bonuses
 \, stipends\, or other incentives\, they must include them in the calculat
 ion of overtime pay\,” said Wage and Hour Division District Director Jua
 n Herrera in Indianapolis. “We encourage employers\, especially those wh
 o offer various types of incentive pay\, to review our compliance assistan
 ce materials and contact us with any questions about overtime requirements
 .”Toa (USA) LLC\, with manufacturing facilities in Mooresville\, is the 
 primary body structure and suspension components supplier for Subaru of In
 diana Automotive and Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing North Americ
 a.Employees and employers can contact the Wage and Hour Division with ques
 tions and requests for compliance assistance at its toll-free helpline\,
  866-4US-WAGE (487-9243). Employers are encouraged to use the agency’s i
 ndustry-specific compliance assistance toolkits to learn about their res
 ponsibilities under the laws enforced by the division. The agency’s PAI
 D program offers employers an opportunity to self-report and resolve pote
 ntial minimum wage and overtime violations under the FLSA\, as well as cer
 tain potential violations under the Family and Medical Leave Act.Learn mor
 e about the Wage and Hour Division\, including a search tool that workers 
 can use if they believe they may be owed back wages collected by the divis
 ion. Download the agency’s free WorkWise Timesheet app f\nhttp://www.d
 ol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20261028
URL:http://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20261028
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
