SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Darby Sabin v. Shawn D. Newcomb et al.
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT Reporter of Decisions \nDecision:
   2026 ME 103 \nDocket: Fra-25-550 \nArgued: September 8\, 2026 \nDecided:
   October 22\, 2026 \n \nPanel:  STANFILL\, C.J.\, and MEAD\, CONNORS\, LA
 WRENCE\, DOUGLAS\, LIPEZ\, and TAUB\, JJ.  \n \n \nDARBY SABIN \n \nv. \n 
 \nSHAWN D. NEWCOMB et al. \n \n \nCONNORS\, J. \n[¶1]  Darby Sabin appeal
 s from an order of the Superior Court (Franklin \nCounty\, Mills\, A.R.J.)
  dismissing her complaint against Shawn Newcomb\, Cynthia \nSoucy\, and Ow
 en Soucy.  After careful review\, we hold that Darby’s\n1 complaint \nsu
 fficiently alleges a claim for tortious interference with an expectancy of
  \ninheritance.  We therefore vacate the dismissal and remand for further 
 \nproceedings consistent with this opinion. \n \n1  Due to the shared last
  names of multiple parties\, we refer to them throughout by their first \n
 names. \n 2 \nI.  BACKGROUND \nA. Factual History \n[¶2]  The following f
 acts are drawn from the factual allegations in the \ncomplaint\, and\, at 
 the motion to dismiss stage\, these allegations are viewed in \nthe light 
 most favorable to the plaintiff.   See Meridian Med . Sys. LLC.\, v. Epix 
 \nTherapeutics\, Inc.\, 2021 ME 24\, ¶ 2\, 250 A.3d 122. \n[¶3]  Steven 
 Sabin\, whose estate is at issue here\, had three children: Paul\, \nKelly
 \, and Janice.  Paul predeceased Steven\, leaving behind one daughter\, Da
 rby.  \nSteven also had two stepchildren\, Shawn and Cynthia. \n[¶4]  In 
 early 2022\, as Steven and his wife\, Christine\, began experiencing \ncog
 nitive decline \, Steven executed a will and a �inancial power of attorn
 ey \n(“POA”).  The will nominated Janice and Shawn as joint personal r
 epresentatives \nand provided that Darby would receive what would have bee
 n Paul’s share of \nthe estate.2  The POA appointed Shawn as Steven’s 
 agent and granted Shawn a \nsigni�icant range  of authority.  Among Shaw
 n’s powers were the ability to \ntransfer\, revocably or irrevocably\, a
 ny real\, tangible\, or intangible property.  The \nPOA further granted Sh
 awn the power to give any property to any per\nhttps://www.courts.maine.go
 v/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me103.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me103.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
