SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] US Department of Labor cites Illinois utility
  construction company for repeated exposure to trenching hazards
DESCRIPTION:CHICAGO – The U.S. Department of Labor has cited a Frankfort
 -based utility construction company for repeatedly exposing employees to e
 xcavation safety hazards after federal investigators observed employees wo
 rking in an unprotected trench.The department’s Occupational Safety and 
 Health Administration initiated an investigation of Always Underground LLC
  as part of its National Emphasis Program on Trenching after witnessing em
 ployees working in an unprotected trench deeper than eight feet.OSHA cited
  the employer for three repeat violations for failing to provide workers w
 ith a safe means of egress\, to install a trench protective system that wo
 uld protect against cave-ins\, and to keep excavated or other materials an
 d equipment at least 2 feet from the edge. Additionally\, the agency cited
  the employer for a serious violation for failing to provide workers with 
 protective hardhats against falling objects.In total\, OSHA proposed $380\
 ,664 in penalties.The employer has 15 business days from receipt of its ci
 tations and penalties to comply\, request an informal conference with OSHA
 ’s area director\, or contest the findings before the independent Occupa
 tional Safety and Health Review Commission. Please check the OSHA establis
 hment search page periodically for any changes in the inspection or penalt
 y status.Visit OSHA’s website to learn about keeping workers safe around
  trenching and excavations. Employers can also contact the agency for info
 rmation about OSHA’s compliance assistance resources and for free help o
 n complying with OSHA standards.\nhttp://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osh
 a/osha20261021
URL:http://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osha/osha20261021
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
